# Queue, Contract Ingestion & First-Invoice Approval

When editing the Queue, ingestion flow, upload modal, approvals pages, approval-settings modal, or ingest context, read:

- **`docs/09-contract-ingestion.md`** — full flow: Queue index (Import + Connect) → upload modal → analysis animation → ingest verification workspace (happy + exception paths) → completion state with two CTAs → auto-submitted approval → approval detail (editable critical fields + Invoice|Contract tabs + comments) → approve toast → ApprovalSettingsModal → "All set" success state → View Customer
- **`docs/06-routing.md`** — `/queue`, `/queue/:queueItemId`, `/approvals/invoices/:invoiceId?ingestId=…`
- **`docs/08-mock-data.md`** — ingestion types, queue items, approval policy types, session state shape

## Key rules

1. The **Queue** is the single landing for every signed contract pending ingestion. Sidebar Desk > Queue → `/queue`.
2. **Import** (primary blue button) opens the upload modal — replaces the previous "Upload" button on the Contracts index.
3. **Connect** opens the integrations modal (Salesforce, DocuSign, Ironclad, NetSuite, Workday, HubSpot, PandaDoc) — visual only.
4. File upload UI is non-functional — only the **two sample documents** drive the active prototype flow:
   - Sample 1 = Echo Corp renewal (`QI-2026-0001`, happy path)
   - Sample 2 = Zenith Analytics new business (`QI-2026-0002`, exception path with missing customer + product mapping)
5. Other queue items (`QI-2026-0003`–`QI-2026-0012`) are placeholders representing PDF / API / CPQ / Email sources, In Progress / Ingested / Failed / Rejected states, and Amendment / Early Renewal scenarios. Clicking them renders a placeholder `PlaceholderState` panel.
6. Session-created objects (customer, product plan, queue overrides, approval policy, invoice field overrides) live in `IngestContext` only — refresh resets.
7. `/queue/:queueItemId` is a **standalone route**, NOT inside the customer shell. Breadcrumb: `Queue > Ingest Contract > {document}`.
8. On Finish Ingestion the page MUST: build the ingest result, **auto-submit the first invoice for approval**, mark the queue item as `Ingested`, and render the completion state with two CTAs ("Review First Invoice →" primary, "Open Contract" secondary).
9. Approval Detail layout:
   - LEFT: editable **critical fields** (amount, tax %, invoice date with backdated hint, due date, payment terms, PO number, billing period, memo) + Approval & Context card
   - RIGHT comments rail (sticky)
   - RIGHT-most preview panel with **Invoice | Contract tabs** (zoom + page controls; pages only on Contract tab)
   - Field edits persist into `invoiceFieldOverrides` keyed by invoice ID and feed into the Invoice preview
10. Comments with `@`-tagging use the hardcoded user list (Jordan Kim, Priya Mehta, Alex Nguyen, Marcus Lee, Rachel Torres, Lena Schulz, Sarah Chen).
11. On Approve → toast **"Invoice sent to the customer"** (~2.4s) → IF this approval came from a fresh ingest (`?ingestId=…` in URL) AND `firstApprovalCompletedFor[ingestId]` is false → open `ApprovalSettingsModal` → after save/skip render the **"All set"** success state with `View Customer →` CTA. Otherwise navigate to `/invoices/:invoiceId?from=approvals`.
12. `ApprovalSettingsModal` has three modes: Auto-approve / Always send for approval / Send for approval only if non-standard. Non-standard exposes editable conditions for high TCV (with $ threshold), discount above threshold (with % threshold), custom payment terms, backdated invoices, manual line items.
13. On Reject → invoice status becomes "Cancelled" via `invoiceStatusOverrides`, no toast, no policy modal.
14. Type-only exports (`ApprovalPolicy`, `ApprovalPolicyMode`, `NonStandardConditions`, `InvoiceFieldOverrides`, `QueueItemOverride`) live in `src/data/approval-policy.ts` to keep `IngestContext.tsx` HMR-clean.
